+# B10 preparation disposition (awaiting independent review)
+
+The exact copied SDD records retain their original text and verdicts. `preparation-copy-map.json` maps every original/destination path, byte count and SHA256, distinguishing exact reports/ledgers from rebased design/GTM documents. `preparation-link-audit.json` checks153 local design/GTM links at the versioned destinations, including referenced fragments. This is a preparation snapshot throughR92, not the final tuple, final evidence/review index, or authority to clean the ignored workspace.
+
+- B07a M1: retained tests now use explicit digest-bound corpus selectors and verified copies. The fresh copy passed17 existing actual replay tests; a new historical-cell adaptation was correctly refused because its compound producer identity is not a clean current Source SHA. The corpus remains a separately retained prerequisite; no fresh-clone success without it.
+- B04b/B07b color warnings: test child environments choose one color policy. Lab build uses pnpm for the nested brand check, removing the mixed npm invocation. Historical warning logs remain unchanged. Lab production build exposed four JSON-import-attribute warnings in model-validation/navigation2d imports; those two owning modules now match the existing browser import convention, and the subsequent build has no such warnings. No physics rerun was performed solely for cleanup.
+- B07b timing: new capture records clock origins, exact browser active-window boundaries and action/run/tick-response correlation. Performance validity/targets derive from raw samples. Old benchmark values remain tied to their original producer tuples; new final capture is pending.
+- B07b390px stripe: prepared browser capture writes simultaneous header DOM/count and screenshot in the live-report replay flow. No new screenshot result or cause claim is made in tooling.
+- B08 M1: new coherent goal/frame mutations pass upstream integrity and reach semantic equivalence rejection. Existing stale-seal world/adjacent-physics fixtures are explicitly named corruption tests. The remaining broader coherent-world/adjacent-physics coverage is deferred to final triage; the nine reviewed profile/model regressions remain intact.
+- L01-R1-05: restore frozen0.14m acceptance in the new checker revision, separately from commanded0.15m; synthetic threshold regression covers both sides. Historical reader pins/evidence remain immutable.
+- L02 lint: five frozen scripts are preserved byte-for-byte; narrow environment/CommonJS overrides fix their27 diagnostics. The full lint result is recorded separately from earlier failed attempts.
+- B00/B01 legacy review detail, B04a dense verifier/diagnostic output, B05 timeout and vendor whitespace, L00 negative-fixture precision, L03 negative zero and L04 oversized trace/oracle bounds remain explicit in the copied central index and original task reports. They are not silently closed by this document.
+- L03-R1-05/native contact/controller gates, WEB05/image execution, HTTPS, commissioning and hardware remain separate unmet qualification gates. Prepared code and static/synthetic tests do not satisfy them.
+
+Final retention must refresh B10/L06 reports and independent reviews, raw decision counts, final ancestry review bases, candidate identities, destination link audit and every deferred disposition before cleanup. Original fork/frozen-upstream merge boundaries and B00/B01 ledger-only review limitations stay in the retained records. Large imported binary patches remain reproducible by exact-ref/argv/hash indexes rather than being duplicated here.
